// Unused-export report for @excitedjs/dreamux's src/ tree (code organization
// refactor, H5). Report-only for this stage: every issue type this config
// scopes to is severity "warn" (printed, not counted toward Knip's total
// error count), so a clean `npm run lint` run still exits 0 no matter how
// many findings this reports. That is Knip's own fine-grained mechanism for
// non-failing mode (see "Rules" in Knip's docs), matching the severity-level
// approach `.dependency-cruiser.cjs` already uses for the R5 layering gate,
// rather than the blunter `--no-exit-code` CLI flag. Raise these to "error"
// once stage 2's deletions land and the noise this first pass reports has
// been triaged (the audit names several dead exports for stage-2 deletion,
// not this stage).
//
// `--include` (wired in package.json's lint script via the `--exports`
// shortcut) already restricts analysis to exactly the issue types listed in
// `rules` below; unused files/dependencies/binaries are a different check
// (not H5's job) and stay entirely unscoped here.
//
// No `project` field here: package.json's lint script passes
// `--use-tsconfig-files`, so tsconfig.tests.json's own `include` (src/ +
// tests/, not tsconfig.json's src/-only scope) is the one owner of which
// files this check scans, instead of a second, hand-copied glob list that
// could drift out of sync with it. `--use-tsconfig-files` also feeds every
// matched file into Knip's real TypeScript program instead of parsing them
// standalone, which resolves cross-file type-level usage a plain glob misses
// (verified empirically: 67 unused-export findings against this codebase
// today, vs 76 from an equivalent glob-based `project` list) — closer to
// this item's own goal of not reporting false positives, on top of scanning
// tests/ so exports only consumed by tests/ (e.g. the `DEFAULT_*` provider
// constants core tests import) aren't flagged either. `entry` allowlists
// this package's two published/semi-public surfaces so their own top-level
// exports are never flagged just because nothing inside the package imports
// them: `server.ts` is the npm `main` entry point, and `service/index.ts` is
// the surface `smoke-built-cli` asserts.
{
  "$schema": "https://unpkg.com/knip@6/schema-jsonc.json",
  "entry": ["src/server.ts", "src/service/index.ts"],
  "rules": {
    "exports": "warn",
    "nsExports": "warn",
    "types": "warn",
    "nsTypes": "warn",
    "enumMembers": "warn",
    "namespaceMembers": "warn",
    "duplicates": "warn",
  },
}
